(Letter from the Chair and Chief Executive) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(FY25 was a year of steady growth for Harbourline Retail. Sales revenue rose 5.6% to A$138.6) Tj T*
(million, compared with A$131.2 million in FY24. Earnings before interest and tax \(EBIT\)) Tj T*
(increased to A$6.9 million from A$6.1 million, and net profit after tax \(NPAT\) was A$4.3) Tj T*
(million, up from A$3.8 million.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Online channels continued to grow. Click and collect and home delivery together accounted) Tj T*
(for 28.1% of orders in FY25, up from 24.7% in FY24. Click and collect orders met the 2-hour) Tj T*
(picking standard 91% of the time.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The Board has declared a fully franked final dividend of 6.5 cents per share, bringing the) Tj T*
(full-year dividend to 11.0 cents per share \(FY24: 10.0 cents\).) Tj T*
